  data: {
    LLM: '1. First deal: the player with the double-six tile leads it. Later deals: turn to start passes right; starter may lead any tile. 2. Each player in turn adds a tile to the layout (same number to touching end). If unable to play, pass (e.g. knock). 3. Round ends when one player plays their last tile (domino) or all four pass (blocked). 4. Milo scoring: winning partnership gets one point for domino; blocked round won by partnership with smallest total pips (one point); if the tile that made domino leaves both ends of the train in the same suit, partnership scores two points (Milo). First partnership to five points wins the game.',
    Player: '1. First deal: the player with the double-six tile leads it. Later deals: turn to start passes right; starter may lead any tile. 2. Each player in turn adds a tile to the layout (same number to touching end). If unable to play, pass (e.g. knock). 3. Round ends when one player plays their last tile (domino) or all four pass (blocked). 4. Milo scoring: winning partnership gets one point for domino; blocked round won by partnership with smallest total pips (one point); if the tile that made domino leaves both ends of the train in the same suit, partnership scores two points (Milo). First partnership to five points wins the game.',
    objective: 'Your partnership wins the game by being the first to reach five points. Points are scored for winning a round (domino or blocked round) and for a Milo (both ends of the train in the same suit when going out).',
    gameplay: '1. First deal: the player with the double-six tile leads it. Later deals: turn to start passes right; starter may lead any tile. 2. Each player in turn adds a tile to the layout (same number to touching end). If unable to play, pass (e.g. knock). 3. Round ends when one player plays their last tile (domino) or all four pass (blocked). 4. Milo scoring: winning partnership gets one point for domino; blocked round won by partnership with smallest total pips (one point); if the tile that made domino leaves both ends of the train in the same suit, partnership scores two points (Milo). First partnership to five points wins the game.',
    keyRules: [
      'Tiles form a single line, end to end; doubles played at right angles. Same number must match at touching ends.',
      'Must play if legally possible; otherwise pass.',
      'Blocked round: team with lower pip total on unplayed tiles wins the round and scores one point.',
